sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: fleet maintenance redesign (recipe.json read by Ansible, selected packages held). docs/cli/node/converge.mdx. Phases: input, agent, software, roles, tools, network, check; network applies hub first, then the Node and waits for the handshake.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: node:converge
  %% kind: node.converge
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant H as VPN hub<br/>WireGuard peers
  CLI->>GW: node:converge NODE
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:converge NODE`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> [--base | --roles=a,b] [--full] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  Note over GW: Validate, reserve targets
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - access follows the [shared Node authority rule](/cli/node) (`NodeAccessAuthorizer`)
  %%> - admission uses recorded Node, role, Tool and network state; no live preflight
  %%> - Node convergence, role addition or convergence, enrollment and agent rekey share one Node admission lock; enrollment's role work stays inside its parent run
  alt unknown Node
    %% path: unknown-node
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>http.404
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no Operation, run or Node change
  else caller refused
    %% path: caller-refused
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>node_access.required
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no Operation, run or Node change
  else unsupported Node
    %% path: unsupported-node
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>node.converge_unsupported
    %%> Requirements:
    %%> - the target must be an active, managed Linux Node
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no Operation, run or Node change
  else selected role not assigned
    %% path: unassigned-role
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>validation.failed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no Operation, run, role assignment or Node change
  else target or hub busy
    %% path: target-busy
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>operation.target_busy
    %%> Result:
    %%> - no new Operation or run; the existing holder keeps its reservation
  else admitted
    %% path: admitted
    opt --base
      %% path: base-scope
      Note over GW: Select base scope
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - narrows the admitted intent, without adding or removing assignments
    end
    opt --roles=a,b
      %% path: selected-roles
      Note over GW: Select recorded roles
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - narrows the admitted intent to the selected assignments
    end
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-converge
    %%> Inputs:
    %%> - the phase digests the Node records; admission clears the record, and `--full` or a recorded failed agent pin sends none; a scoped run holds a record that a full converge wrote for its result (docs/reference/node-provisioning.md#skip-a-phase-whose-input-did-not-change)
    %%> - target, scope, recorded roles, Tools, network and vault key names; playbooks read release pins
    %%> - the Gateway includes a CLI plan only for a Node with a recorded `ci-runner` assignment that is not being removed; scope flags do not change that decision
    %%> - reserve the Node and its recorded hub until the Operation settles; two converges of different peers of the hub pass each other, whatever their scope (each writes the same recorded peer set to the hub); beside a converge of the hub Node itself, only two base converges pass (a base intent has no network)
    %%> - automatic release role work waits for Instance and task Operations that participate on its target Node
    %%> - the seven Ansible plays lock a behavior per Node (`node-converge-converge-<phase>-<node_id>`), so converges of different Nodes run side by side
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>Operation ID
    %%> Result:
    %%> - execution continues asynchronously under the admitted Operation
    SW->>SW: Prepare the input<br/>phase: input
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - writes private inventory, vars and known_hosts from schema-validated inputs
    %%> - stages the shipped Ansible files and Tool helper in the private run folder shared by the Swamp Node workers
    %%> - after it writes the input files for the phases, computes each phase digest from what the phases read: those files with the Operation ID masked, the Ansible bundle and the Tool helper with its Tool files; lists the phases whose digest equals the record
    opt digest equals the record
      %% path: phase-unchanged
      Note over SW: Skip an unchanged phase
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - the phase does not run and does not read the Node; the result shows it `unchanged`, with no changes and no time
      %%> - drift is not an input: the check phase still reads the Node, and `--full` runs every phase
    end
    SW->>N: Install Orbit's layer<br/>Ansible phase: agent
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - applies the agent, Orbit-owned files and units, and the kernel policy (SCTP blocked, non-local bind); restarts only changed services
    %%> - writes the units the Node's roles own (the Swamp worker template, the websocket unit) and reloads systemd; it never starts or restarts them, and never writes the Swamp serve unit
    %%> - with a CLI plan: requires and installs its pinned release and root profile
    %%> - without a CLI plan: needs no CLI release or probe; removes the managed `/usr/local/bin/orbit` link, regular `orbit-0.N.0` binaries and root profile at `/root/.orbit/config.json` in this phase, under the Node update lock; preserves unrelated executables, backups and directories
    SW->>N: Install pinned software<br/>Ansible phase: software
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads recipe.json and holds its selected packages at their pins
    SW->>N: Configure the roles<br/>Ansible phase: roles
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - repairs selected role configuration without changing an Instance or role assignment
    %%> - on a Node that offers proof places, other than the proof default's Node: first reads root's Incus client certificate on the default's Node, as `node:role:converge` does, and writes the seed listener's trust; on any other Node with `ci-runner` it removes the trust and stops the listener; it never opens the listener or changes its firewall rules (docs/reference/node-provisioning.md#the-seed-listener)
    %%> - on an app-dev Node: writes each Instance container's presented machine name (`/etc/hostname`, `PRETTY_HOSTNAME` in `/etc/machine-info`, the `127.0.1.1` line of `/etc/hosts`) through the file API, running, stopped or frozen; nothing restarts, so the kernel hostname follows at the container's next start and T3's label at T3's next start
    SW->>N: Apply recorded Tools<br/>Ansible phase: tools
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - runs the Tool helper once on the Swamp Node, before it judges a Tool
    %%> On a helper that cannot run:
    %%> - fail the phase and mark no Tool failed
    %%> On a Tool failure:
    %%> - continue with the other Tools and mark only that Tool failed
    alt recorded network in scope
      %% path: recorded-network
      SW->>H: Apply hub network<br/>Ansible phase: network
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - applies the recorded hub side before the peer; matching configuration is unchanged
      %%> - prunes only the peer files of Nodes that are gone or being removed, decided when the prune runs: it keeps every Node of the snapshot and every file above the snapshot's newest Node id, so a task VM that joins while the run waits keeps its peer
      %%> - removes the task VM hub filter that the removed `task_vm.hub_converge` left: stops and disables `orbit-task-vms-hub.service`, deletes its unit file and `/etc/orbit/task-vms/hub.nft`, and deletes the nft table `inet orbit_task_vms`; deletes every UFW rule whose comment starts with `orbit:task-vm-` by its spec from `ufw show added`, never by number, and no other rule, so two peer converges that run it together cannot delete a live rule; a hub without the filter or those rules changes nothing
      %%> - on the hub: carries the mark in `wg syncconf`, opens SSH on its LAN address to its /24, adds the routed rule `orbit:vpn-peer-forwarding` (in and out on `orbit`, from the VPN subnet to the VPN subnet; UFW skips the same rule added by hand), writes the source unit (`orbit-hub-source.service`), restarts it on change or drift, and checks that a marked packet to a public address leaves from the public endpoint address; an IPv4 endpoint the hub does not hold fails the phase with the assertion `vpn.endpoint_not_local`
      SW->>N: Apply peer, wait<br/>Ansible phase: network
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - when the rendered hub endpoint is the hub's LAN address, first proves that the kernel routes it directly from the Node's `lan_ip` and that an SSH host key there has the hub's recorded fingerprint; a failed proof fails the phase before any WireGuard change, with the assertion `node.hub_lan_unreachable` or `node.hub_lan_identity_mismatch`, with no fallback to the public endpoint
      %%> - a changed hub endpoint, read from the previous `orbit.peers`, moves in one detached job on the Node: it takes WireGuard packets only from the new endpoint's address while it runs (assertion `node.hub_switch_unpinned` when it cannot), installs the staged files, ends the old session and accepts only a handshake from after the move; without one, it puts the previous files back and loads them, and the phase fails with the assertion `node.hub_switch_no_handshake`; when `wg` does not load the new files, it puts the previous ones back at once, and the assertion is `node.hub_switch_load_failed`
      %%> - applies the recorded Node side and waits for the tunnel handshake
      %%> - both arrows are one phase; the peer arrow is only for a peer target
      %%> - a target hub is applied once; it requires every recorded peer on its interface (assertion `vpn.hub_peer_missing`) and waits only for the peers that had a handshake in the 120 seconds before the change, each for a handshake in the last 180 seconds, so an offline peer does not fail it
    else no recorded network in scope
      %% path: no-recorded-network
      Note over SW: Network: no peer change<br/>Ansible phase: network
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the phase has no recorded configuration or handshake to apply
    end
    SW->>N: Check the Node<br/>Ansible phase: check
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - checks the selected software, units and role configuration, plus the recorded tunnel; on a target hub, every recorded peer on its interface, with no handshake wait
    %%> - checks the pinned CLI only when the Gateway supplied a CLI plan; otherwise checks that the managed CLI files are absent
    %%> - the phases run in order, idempotently; an empty scope item needs no mutation; input and check always run
    opt phases completed or failed
      %% path: cleanup
      SW->>SW: Remove private run files
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - declared cleanup waits for Node work to stop and removes only this run's files
      %%> - preserve the original failure and expose incomplete cleanup; interruption proves no cleanup
    end
    alt end check passes
      %% path: succeeded
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal result
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the shared reader marks the Operation succeeded and records each Tool's result
      %%> - with `ci-runner` in scope, records the seed listener in `nodes.seed_sender_id`: it keeps the sender it names when the intent names the same sender, and clears it otherwise (docs/reference/node-provisioning.md#the-seed-listener)
      %%> - with `ci-runner` in scope, records the hold script in `nodes.ci_hold_digest`: it keeps the digest when it is the digest of the script in the intent, and clears it otherwise; it keeps `nodes.ci_nested_hosting` only when the intent carries the nested branch (docs/reference/node-provisioning.md#proof-places-on-a-ci-node)
      %%> - the result lists each Instance container that got no Chromium trust store, with its reason
      %%> - a full-scope run records each phase digest on the Node, whether the phase ran or was unchanged; a scoped run keeps the full-converge record it held at admission without the phases it changed, and without `network` when its network phase ran with a hub
      %%> - a repeat is another Operation, not an admission skip; its unchanged phases skip; with `--full`, matching tasks report zero changes
    else a phase fails
      %% path: phase-failed
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code · failed step
      %%> Result:
      %%> - stop at the failed phase and mark the Operation failed; later phases do not run
      %%> - with `ci-runner` in scope, records the seed listener as on success when the roles phase passed, and clears `nodes.seed_sender_id` when it did not
      %%> - with `ci-runner` in scope, records the hold script as on success when the roles phase passed, and clears `nodes.ci_hold_digest` and `nodes.ci_nested_hosting` when it did not
      %%> - the result names the earliest fatal task among hosts whose statistics fail: each host contributes its last failed or unreachable record; ties select hub; names are bounded and may be withheld
      %%> - censored-only evidence from a failed host reports a hidden task; missing, malformed or task-free reports leave `failure` absent; private callback output stays private
      %%> - unreachable targets fail here, not at a live admission check
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - completed and partial changes remain; no rollback and no Instance or assignment change
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - the Node keeps no phase digest, so a new attempt starts at input and reapplies every phase safely
    end
  end
